//    probable degenerate output; penalizing "c" forces the R-group to start aliphatic,
//    exposing the much larger aliphatic diversity space (chain length, branching,
//    halogenation, cycloalkyl ring size).
// 3. Raise mid-phase temperature to 2.0 (from 1.6) to flatten the conditional
//    distribution over valid aliphatic R-group completions.
// 4. Updated guidance shows 25 diverse structures from 7 structural classes.
//
// Why this should reach 36%: aliphatic isocyanates (methyl, ethyl, propyl, butyl,
// pentyl, isopropyl, tert-butyl, isobutyl, cyclopropyl, cyclobutyl, cyclopentyl,
// cyclohexyl, fluoromethyl, chloromethyl, allyl, propargyl, …) have substantially
// more unique valid members than the aromatic set, so even moderate temperature
// spread over the aliphatic space yields more unique valid molecules per 100 runs.
